WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.026
Teachers can get free packages of printable
logic puzzles, made for their class.

2
00:00:06.376 --> 00:00:12.393
This short video shows every step, from the
request form to the PDFs in your inbox.

3
00:00:13.443 --> 00:00:19.054
On thelogicgrid.com, choose For educators, at
the top of the game page.

4
00:00:20.104 --> 00:00:23.347
The Educators page explains the four steps.

5
00:00:23.697 --> 00:00:26.719
Fill in the form, confirm your school email,

6
00:00:26.739 --> 00:00:31.314
our team reviews your request, and your
puzzles arrive by email.

7
00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:36.823
Start with your name, your school email
address, your school and your role.

8
00:00:37.173 --> 00:00:40.220
Use your school address, not a personal one:

9
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.363
we send a code there to confirm that you are
an educator.

10
00:00:45.413 --> 00:00:47.782
Choose your students' grade level.

11
00:00:48.132 --> 00:00:51.739
The page shows what suits that grade: the
difficulty,

12
00:00:51.759 --> 00:00:57.178
the size of the grid, how much story to read,
and whether to use large print.

13
00:00:58.228 --> 00:01:02.005
Then say how many different puzzles you need,
up to thirty.

14
00:01:02.355 --> 00:01:05.214
Choose the difficulty: suited to the grade,

15
00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:09.737
building up from easier to harder, or one
level for every puzzle.

16
00:01:10.087 --> 00:01:12.398
You can also choose the grid size,

17
00:01:12.418 --> 00:01:17.298
how many questions go under each puzzle, and
even the kinds of clues.

18
00:01:18.348 --> 00:01:23.874
Pick any of our themes, with a topic for each,
or tick none for a mix of them all.

19
00:01:24.224 --> 00:01:26.884
You can type your students' first names, too,

20
00:01:26.904 --> 00:01:29.793
and they become the characters in the stories.

21
00:01:30.843 --> 00:01:33.041
Or choose Create my own theme.

22
00:01:33.391 --> 00:01:36.617
Start from an example, or write your own
story,

23
00:01:36.637 --> 00:01:40.794
characters and up to four categories, each
with its items.

24
00:01:41.144 --> 00:01:45.021
We build the grid, the clues and the answer
key from it,

25
00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:48.739
and check that every puzzle has exactly one
answer.

26
00:01:49.789 --> 00:01:53.898
Under Printing, choose the paper size, where
the answer keys go,

27
00:01:53.918 --> 00:01:57.939
worked solutions, large print, and a title for
your package.

28
00:01:58.989 --> 00:02:03.185
Tick the box to agree to use the puzzles with
your own students,

29
00:02:03.205 --> 00:02:05.134
then press Send my request.

30
00:02:06.184 --> 00:02:10.793
The page now asks for a six-digit code. Check
your school email.

31
00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:17.155
The email has your code, and a button that
confirms your address in one click.

32
00:02:17.505 --> 00:02:20.969
The code works for two days. If it does not
arrive,

33
00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:24.418
look in your spam folder, or ask for a new
code.

34
00:02:25.468 --> 00:02:27.666
Type the code and press Confirm.

35
00:02:28.716 --> 00:02:34.626
That's it. Your request is now with our team,
and the page gives you a request number.

36
00:02:35.676 --> 00:02:41.565
A person on our team checks each request,
usually within a day or two, and approves it.

37
00:02:42.615 --> 00:02:48.164
Once it is approved, your puzzles are made and
emailed to you within minutes,

38
00:02:48.184 --> 00:02:50.359
as PDF files ready to print.

39
00:02:51.409 --> 00:02:57.298
Each package starts with a cover page: how to
use the puzzles, and a list of them all.

40
00:02:58.348 --> 00:03:03.600
Every puzzle has a brand new story, written at
the right level for the grade,

41
00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:06.989
with the clues, a blank grid and the
questions.

42
00:03:08.039 --> 00:03:12.425
The answer keys come in their own file, so you
can keep them back,

43
00:03:12.445 --> 00:03:15.933
with a step by step solution if you asked for
one.

44
00:03:16.983 --> 00:03:21.741
The email with your puzzles also has a private
link to your own ideas,

45
00:03:21.761 --> 00:03:23.959
problems and feedback section.

46
00:03:24.309 --> 00:03:29.025
It starts with a two-minute survey about how
our tools can help your class.

47
00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:35.921
Send us an idea, a problem or feedback any
time, and see our answers right there.

48
00:03:36.971 --> 00:03:42.369
Our team reads every note, answers in plain
words, and emails you the answer.

49
00:03:43.419 --> 00:03:47.771
Fill in the form, confirm your email, and
print. Happy puzzling!

